{'id': 'arc_task_e262a407_rule_extend_multi_cell_diagonal_colors_into_rays', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-e262a407 rule: extend multi-cell diagonal colors into rays', 'content': "task-e262a407 SOLVED (2 wrong). RULE: small cluster of colored cells on uniform background. For EACH COLOR separately: if a color has >=2 cells forming a diagonal segment, extend that diagonal as a ray of the same color, continuing away from the rest of the cluster, one cell per step, until the grid edge. Colors with only ONE cell (and colors whose cells are only horizontal/vertical pairs) do NOT extend at all. Extension starts one step beyond the outermost cell of the segment, on the side pointing away from the other colors. Examples seen: 2-cell diagonal wings extended up-left/up-right; 3-cell corner (horizontal pair + diagonal) extended along its diagonal subset; single-cell 'tip' colors (even 2 different single-cell colors forming a horizontal tip pair) never extended. Wrong guesses: extending single-cell colors by quadrant-from-centroid; extending only 'wing' colors including a single-cell one.", 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-28T13:33:51.076158+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-28T13:33:51.076179+00:00', 'version': 1}

