{'id': 'arc_task_e262a407_rule_apex_cells_fixed_leg_rays_extend_away_to_edges', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-e262a407 rule: apex cells fixed, leg rays extend away to edges', 'content': 'ARC task-e262a407 in progress. RULE v2: pattern = apex/marker cells + diagonal leg rays. Apex color cells NEVER extend. Leg rays (same-color diagonal runs) extend AWAY from apex until grid edge or different color. Demo1: apex 8-8, legs 7 (down-left), 4 (down-right) extended to edges. Demo2: block 8,4,6,7 with 6-ray extended down-left; 8 did not extend up-left. Test: apex=9s at (22,2),(23,3); 4-ray up-right to (20,5); 1-ray already at edge. First submission failed by wrongly extending 9s both directions.', 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-28T18:30:06.353274+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-28T18:30:06.353309+00:00', 'version': 1}

