{'id': 'arc_task_e262a407_solved_apex_cells_fixed_leg_rays_extend_away_to_edges', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-e262a407 SOLVED: apex cells fixed, leg rays extend away to edges', 'content': "ARC task-e262a407 SOLVED (2 demos, 1 wrong attempt). FAMILY 'apex + diagonal leg rays': background = dominant uniform color. Pattern = apex/marker cells (recolor anchor, NEVER extend) + leg rays: same-color diagonal runs that extend AWAY from the apex along their diagonal until grid edge or a different-colored cell. Single cells adjacent to apex that begin rays are part of the ray if they continue the diagonal away from apex. RULE v1 (extend every diagonal run len>=2 in both directions) was WRONG - it wrongly extended apex-colored cells. Correct: identify apex first (in test: the 9s at (22,2),(23,3) diagonal pair; in demo1: horizontal 8-8 pair; in demo2: single 8 top-left of 2x2 block). Leg colors extend one direction only, away from apex. Cost: 2 demos + 1 wrong submission.", 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-28T18:30:21.255025+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-28T18:30:21.255044+00:00', 'version': 1}

