== arc_task_3c58f95d_rule_colored_lines_extend_as_periodic_stripes_period_line_coun
{'id': 'arc_task_3c58f95d_rule_colored_lines_extend_as_periodic_stripes_period_line_coun', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-3c58f95d rule: colored lines extend as periodic stripes (period = line count)', 'content': "task-3c58f95d SOLVED 1st try (0 wrong, 1 demo). RULE: input has full 1-cell-wide colored lines (diagonal anti-diagonals or horizontal rows) on 0 background. Output: extend each line's color periodically across the whole grid. Period = number of colored lines. For each cell, color = color of the line whose index position mod period matches (line_index mod period). Equivalently: out(r,c)=P[(r+c) mod n] for diagonal lines (P built from line sums mod n), or out(r,c)=Q[r mod n] for horizontal lines (Q built from line row indices mod n). Verify residues mod n are all distinct across lines - that confirms n. Demo (16x16): anti-diagonals at sums 1,6,14,17,27,28 colors 7,1,4,8,1,6 -> P=[1,7,4,1,6,8], out=P[(r+c)%6]. Test (28x28): horizontal rows at 0,7,8,11,21,22 colors 4,9,6,1,6,3 -> Q=[4,9,6,6,3,1] by row%6, out=Q[r%6]. FAMILY: 'periodic line-stripe completion'.", 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-28T21:28:18.562415+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-28T21:28:18.562441+00:00', 'version': 1}

