{'id': 'arc_task_e262a407_rule_corner_rays_from_diagonal_runs', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-e262a407 rule: corner rays from diagonal runs', 'content': "ARC task-e262a407 SOLVED (2 wrong, 3 demos). Background = dominant color; small multi-color shape in an otherwise uniform grid.\n\nRULE: for each maximal diagonal run (slope +1 or -1) of the SAME color with length >= 2, extend a ray along that same diagonal away from the rest of the shape, painting background cells with the run's color, until hitting the grid edge or any non-background cell. Single-cell colors do NOT extend (they act as blockers). If all runs' rays are off-grid or blocked, output = input unchanged.\n\nEvidence: demo1 shape (0s chevron + 6s pair + lone 3) -> 3 rays to edges, lone 3 stayed. Demo2/demo3: solid 2x2 blocks of distinct colors -> unchanged. Test: 7-run at (14,0),(15,1), ray up-left off-grid / down-right blocked by 5 -> output = input.\n\nWRONG guesses (cost 2): (a) treating single cells (3/4/5) as corner/ray emitters; (b) treating color 3 as special anchor emitting a ray. Only length>=2 same-color diagonal runs emit rays.", 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-28T21:45:58.267286+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-28T21:45:58.267306+00:00', 'version': 1}

