{'id': 'arc_task_3c58f95d_rule_horizontal_line_grid_vertical_tiling_by_line_count_period', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-3c58f95d rule: horizontal line grid -> vertical tiling by line-count period', 'content': 'task-3c58f95d SOLVED (1 demo, 0 wrong). RULE: input has a few full-width horizontal colored lines on 0 background. Output = vertical tiling of the input grid with period p = number of colored lines (also: minimal p such that all colored row indices are distinct mod p and residues cover 0..p-1). Output row i = color of the colored line whose row index == i mod p. Demo: lines at rows 1(8),5(2),8(5),9(2),10(2),12(2) -> p=6, period pattern [2,8,5,2,2,2] tiled. Test 28x28: lines rows 0(5),4(3),20(7) -> p=3, rows cycle [5,3,7].', 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-28T22:10:31.057701+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-28T22:10:31.057722+00:00', 'version': 1}

