{'id': 'arc_task_b11169f1_rule_block_downsample_colored_cells_global', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-b11169f1 rule: block-downsample colored cells (global)', 'content': "task-b11169f1 SOLVED (0 wrong, 1 demo). FAMILY 'block downsample': input grid with noise color 5 and background 0, scattered small shapes of 1-2 other colors. RULE: divide input into k x k tiles where k = input_dim / output_dim (demo: 18x18 -> 6x6, k=3; test: 12x12 -> 4x4, k=3). Each output cell = the color found in that tile if the tile contains any cell of a non-0, non-noise(5) color, else 0. If a tile had multiple colors (didn't occur here), pick any/first. Output dims = input dims divided by tile size; when input dim divisible by both 2 and 3, prefer k=3 (worked here). Detection: output grid much smaller than input; noise color 5 scattered everywhere.", 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-28T23:52:25.319092+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-28T23:52:25.319115+00:00', 'version': 1}

== arc_task_3c58f95d_rule_diagonal_lines_extended_into_tiled_stripe_pattern
{'id': 'arc_task_3c58f95d_rule_diagonal_lines_extended_into_tiled_stripe_pattern', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC task-3c58f95d rule: diagonal lines extended into tiled stripe pattern', 'content': "task-3c58f95d SOLVED (1 demo, 0 wrong). FAMILY 'diagonal stripe tiling': input grid contains a few short colored diagonal lines (cells on constant i+j or constant i-j); background 0 elsewhere. RULE: extend the pattern over the whole grid. Let L = number of distinct diagonal lines (line groups by their constant diagonal index; corner-triangle cells each count as their own line). Order lines by diagonal index and tile the grid with period L: cell (i,j) gets the color of the line whose index == (i+j) mod L (or (i-j) mod L for main-direction lines). Equivalently each color fills anti-diagonals congruent to its line mod (number of lines). EXAMPLE test: 4 anti-diagonal lines at i+j = 2(7), 23(1), 29(3), 32(5) -> period 4, residues mod4: 0->5, 1->3, 2->7, 3->1. Demo: 3 main-diagonal lines i-j = -9(3), -8(3), 2(7) -> period 3, residue 2->7 else 3. Note period = number of line groups, NOT number of colors. Verify output preserves all nonzero input cells before submitting.", 'path': 'general', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-10-29T01:06:26.449357+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-29T01:06:26.449381+00:00', 'version': 1}

